WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.700
Generators mode gives you four function generators.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.229
Graph mode is a node engine with more than fifty node types.

3
00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:09.523
Switch the Modulation section to Graph.

4
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:16.771
Beginner view looks like the function generators, but each row is a real node with a binding.

5
00:00:16.771 --> 00:00:19.402
Click Add patch: an LFO into Z Push.

6
00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.437
Change its source to Noise.

7
00:00:21.437 --> 00:00:24.079
White noise jitters the depth on every frame.

8
00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:27.500
Point it at Rotation instead, and turn the amount up.

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.126
Now the whole raster shivers.

10
00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:30.665
Add a second row.

11
00:00:30.665 --> 00:00:34.414
A Ramp, sweeping H Size from narrow to wide, over and over.

12
00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:36.957
The Library holds ready-made patches.

13
00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:40.956
Load Getting Started, a slow breathing depth with a note explaining it.

14
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:47.166
Both mode runs the function generators and the graph together, so switching never throws your patches away.

15
00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:50.419
Beginner view covers simple one-to-one patches.

16
00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:53.699
Next, the Advanced canvas, where nodes feed each other.
